       "text": "I'm sorry, but I won't enter ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily, even with your confirmation. The total of 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum adult daily dose. It has no established indication, and it carries a serious risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. A normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change that.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily (3,200 mg/day).** This is the highest standard dose. I can add a note such as \"dose capped at max; prescriber requested higher.\"\n- **Enter a different dose or frequency** that you choose within the labeled range.\n- **Help you reach pharmacy or another prescriber.** If you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, a pharmacist or toxicology consult can review it. Another analgesic or adjunct might also work better.\n\nLet me know which you'd like."
